><p>Tree-of-Thoughts generates multiple nodes at each level, and it evaluat=
es them with a scorer to keep only expanding =E2=80=9Cthe good ones=E2=80=
=9D for efficiency. At the end, it evaluates the leaf nodes to select the f=
inal answer.</p><p>(Note that the figure is relatively simple in terms of b=
ranching complexity to make it fit. However, the fact that it is unbalanced=
 is intentional. Tree-of-Thoughts does not usually produce a fixed number o=
f branches per node. Instead, the branching factor varies depending on prun=
ing, scoring, and budget constraints, so there may be different numbers of =
children at each step.)</p><h2 class=3D"header-anchor-post"><strong>7.1 Sea=
rch Over Solution Paths Papers (2025)</strong><div class=3D"pencraft pc-dis=
play-flex pc-alignItems-center pc-position-absolute pc-reset header-anchor-=
parent"><div class=3D"pencraft pc-display-contents pc-reset pubTheme-yiXxQA=
