71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p>Of course, we can also combin=
e most of these methods, meaning we can use more than one at a time. Most c=
ombinations are intuitive and further improve performance. However, the mor=
e we combine these methods, the more expensive inference scaling gets.</p><=
p>To provide one of the many example scenarios, we could use self-consisten=
cy as our baseline for solving math problems. For each independent sample i=
n self-consistency, we could use self-refinement over several iterations an=
d then extract the final answer. Additionally, we can use a Best-of-N-style=
 scoring method if there are ties in self-consistency sampling (for instanc=
e, if our possible answers are [4, 4, 2, 3, 2]).</p><h2 class=3D"header-anc=
hor-post"><strong>8.3 The Best Method?</strong><div class=3D"pencraft pc-di=
