=80=99s hard to say if OpenAI uses these techniques for regular prompts. Ho=
wever, at least they use them for their benchmarks. According to the </span=
><a href=3D"https://openai.com/index/learning-to-reason-with-llms/">o1 blog=
</a><span>:</span></p><blockquote><p>o1 averaged 74% (11.1/15) with a singl=
e sample per problem, 83% (12.5/15) with consensus among 64 samples, and 93=
% (13.9/15) when re-ranking 1000 samples with a learned scoring function.</=
p></blockquote><p>Anthropic seems to be even more explicit about the use of=
 self-consistency and Best-of-N in their evaluations:</p><blockquote><p><sp=
an>Our researchers have also been experimenting with improving the model=E2=
=80=99s performance using parallel test-time compute. They do this by sampl=
ing multiple independent thought processes and selecting the best one witho=
ut knowing the true answer ahead of time. One way to do this is with majori=
ty or consensus voting; selecting the answer that appears most commonly as =
the =E2=80=98best=E2=80=99 one. Another is using another language model (li=
ke a second copy of Claude) asked to check its work or a learned scoring fu=
nction and pick what it thinks is best (</span><a href=3D"https://www.anthr=
opic.com/news/visible-extended-thinking">Source</a><span>)</span></p></bloc=
kquote><p><span>Next, from the </span><a href=3D"https://x.ai/news/grok-4">=
Grok 4 blog article</a><span>:</span></p><blockquote><p>We have made furthe=
r progress on parallel test-time compute, which allows Grok to consider mul=
tiple hypotheses at once. We call this model Grok 4 Heavy, and it sets a ne=
w standard for performance and reliability.</p></blockquote><p><span>Gemini=
 also </span><a href=3D"https://x.com/GoogleDeepMind/status/199665840123384=
2624?s=3D20">announced</a><span> in December a mode that sounds just like s=
elf-consistency or Best-of-N:</span></p><blockquote><p><span>We=E2=80=99re =
pushing the boundaries of intelligence even further with Gemini 3 Deep Thin=
k. </span><br><span>This mode meaningfully improves reasoning capabilities =
by exploring many hypotheses simultaneously to solve problems.</span></p></=
